_ENVIRONMENTS.md under \\\"Named measurement hosts\\\", 2026-11-05): 5.00 GiB and 4.54 GiB in two independent runs, 4.28 GiB with source caches warm, always 0 max events; polled anonymous usage peaked at 1.46 GiB, so the peak is page-cache dominated. Baseline 5 GiB (worst observed peak), hard cap 6 GiB (1.2 times that worst; the throttling stops because only the hard cap is enforced as memory.max). The 300-second wall cap (https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3381) was set after a 187-second timeout of the pinned-root twin under load at one core. Nothing in it runs a rust-script: hermit-manifest-plan has no build script, nor does its one path dependency, detcore-model. So since 2026-10-16 it waits only for the pinned Reverie (pre.reverie_pin) and compiles beside build.rust_scripts, which builds in target/ci/rust-script-build rather than target/debug; gate.manifest, the first node that runs both these binaries and the rust-script tools, waits for both. It keeps the rust-script environment, with HERMIT_PREBUILT_RUST_SCRIPTS_REQUIRED=1, so a rust-script added here later fails at once instead of compiling or running unprepared. Until then it waited for build.rust_scripts: in the full validation of hermit 32e1c019 it started 238 s into the run, when build.rust_scripts ended, and took 38 s, and every product node waits on gate.manifest after it.\",\n      \"labels\": [\n        \"quick\",\n        \"super\"\n      ],\n      \"cmd\": \"export PATH=\\\"$PWD/ci/rust-script-bin:$PATH\\\"; export HERMIT_RUST_SCRIPT_ARTIFACT_ROOT=\\\"$PWD/target/ci/rust-scripts\\\"; export HERMIT_PREBUILT_RUST_SCRIPTS_REQUIRED=1; cargo build --locked -p hermit-manifest-plan --bins\",\n      \"result_manifests\": [],\n      \"deps\": [\n        \"pre.reverie_pin\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {},\n      \"networkonly\": false,\n      \"engine_only\": false,\n      \"timeout\": 600,\n      \"cpu_timeout\": 2100,\n      \"priority\": 50,\n      \"jobs_flag\": \"\",\n      \"jobs_env\": \"CARGO_BUILD_JOBS\",\n      \"hint\": {\n        \"resources\": {},\n        \"est_duration_s\": 60.0,\n        \"rss_baseline_bytes\": 5368709120,\n        \"hard_mem_max_bytes\": 6442450944,\n        \"classification\": \"cpu-bound\",\n        \"preferred_inner_jobs\": 8,\n        \"measured_effective_cores\": null,\n        \"measured_cpu_utilization\": null\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"group\": \"quick-super-gate\",\n      \"job\": \"manifest\",\n      \"desc\": \"Centralized test manifest and inventory\",\n      \"description\": \"SELF-TESTS MOVED OUT 2026-09-29: every product node waits on this gate, and the local validation of Hermit 98a621f42935d585e1306262b11d64488dd51614 was killed here by the 900-second CPU cap while the gate was still running repository-tool self-tests. Those self-tests (scorecard, pressure_test, validate_rs, manifest_cli, dbt_budget; TOOL_SELF_TESTS in validation_dag.rs) now run as selftest.<name> leaf nodes that still decide the verdict but block nothing. The gate keeps only what product nodes consume: the manifest-plan audits run in process (DAG/manifest correspondence, budget ordering, determinism-stress evidence, CLI brackets and the expected-cell plan, which define the cells and commands the product nodes execute), and `generate-test-footprints --check`, which proves the committed ci/test-footprints.json still matches ci/dag/validate.json and Cargo metadata, so hosted test selection picks product nodes from current data. Measured 2026-09-29 on the measurement host recorded for gate.manifest in docs/TESTING_ENVIRONMENTS.md (\\\"Named measurement hosts\\\") at load average 215-233: `test-harness validate` took 2.88 s wall and 2.53 CPU seconds (1.99 user, 0.54 system, 29440 KiB largest process RSS), against 664 s of wall before it was killed at 900 CPU seconds with the self-tests included. The 120 CPU seconds are 47 times that sample and bound a hang, not the work; the ordinary and quick/super gates share the constant. The 900-second wall