le. The Step constructor orders these as wall, CPU, then memory. WIDTH 16 AND OVERLAPPED PHASES 2026-10-16: once the clippy pass has passed, ci/prepare-rust-scripts.sh runs the release build beside the test-harness build (Cargo locks release/ and debug/ separately; a clippy failure still stops before either), and the width is 16. Measured cold as transient units at CPUQuota equal to the width, alternating pairs at host load 266-374: the committed sequential producer at width 8 took 196 and 183 s (18.4-19.5 CPU-minutes, peak 4.7 GiB); this one at width 16 took 123 and 128 s (18.4-18.6 CPU-minutes, peak 6.2-6.4 GiB). Width 16 alone, still sequential, took 160 and 175 s in earlier pairs, and overlapping alone at width 8 gained little because the build is CPU-bound there (18-21 CPU-minutes over 8 cores). The hard memory cap goes from 6 to 10 GiB (1.5 times the 6.5-GiB peak seen across these runs, rounded up) and the accounting baseline from 4 to 7 GiB. QUICK/SUPER CPU RE-DERIVATION 2026-11-04: the distinct 1200-second quick/super CPU budget above was sized from a 737.730-second sample predating the width-16 overlapped phases, and the workload has since grown from 28 to 38 entrypoints. A front-door run at Hermit 4627d1d9 in a fresh tool root was CPU-killed above 1200 seconds in 126.53 seconds of wall (about ten cores busy). Remeasured cold that day on the host recorded in docs/TESTING_ENVIRONMENTS.md under \\\"Named measurement hosts\\\" (pristine worktree, warm registry, width 16, host load 61-89): 1415.37 CPU seconds (1319.02 user, 96.35 system) over 147.6 seconds wall. 2400 is the next 300-second bucket above 1.5 times that peak (2123.1). The shared 1200-second wall bound is unchanged: at width 16 the CPU bound stays reachable in 150 seconds of wall. A cold registry (empty CARGO_HOME) cannot run here at all - Cargo cannot reach its registry through this host's proxy - so warm-registry cold-target is the coldest legitimate state this cap sizes for. FRESH-CLONE RE-DERIV